  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade Mission Horticulture &amp; Potato to Nigeria 2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PurposeThe primary goal of the trade mission is to strengthen the bilateral relationship between Nigeria and The Netherlands while enhancing private sector and economic cooperation in the horticulture and potato value chains. It will build on the success stories from previous trade missions in 2024 and 2025, with participants taking part in the Agrofood Fair in Lagos, a critical platform for promoting Dutch expertise and technology.  Through the trade mission the following goals can be achieved within the track &#x2018;Horticulture in Nigeria&#x2019;: &#x2022;	Business to business cooperation between Dutch and Nigerian small- and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) is stimulated/strengthened by networking and matchmaking; &#x2022;	Focus is on trade and investments that benefit people, create jobs and preferably, are accompanied by the transfer of knowledge and skills; and&#x2022;	Through business cooperation, the aim is to enhance food and nutritional security in Nigeria.</narrative>
  </description>
